module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.GlobalSectionSmul
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Coherent.HomColimit.FirstDisplaySurjectivity
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ResolutionsAndBounds.SubmoduleFactorAffine

/-!
# Extending a morphism defined on a principal open, after multiplication by a power

Let `X` be a Noetherian scheme, `f` a global section of `𝒪_X`, `G` a coherent and `F` a
quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module. This file proves that a morphism `θ : G|_{D(f)} ⟶ F|_{D(f)}`
defined only on the principal open `D(f)` extends, after multiplication by a power of `f`, to a
morphism `G ⟶ F` defined on all of `X`.

This is the step of the Stacks proofs that reads "choose `f` not vanishing at `x` with
`D(f) ⊆ V`, extend `φ_V` to `fⁿ ℱ → 𝒢` by [Stacks, Tag 01YB] and precompose with multiplication
by `fⁿ`" — it is what lets a morphism produced on a *neighbourhood* by [Stacks, Tag 01Y4] be fed
to the extension theorem of [Stacks, Tag 01YB], whose conclusion is about the complement of the
support of an ideal sheaf. Both halves of that bridge are supplied here: the identification of
`D(f)` as the complement of the support of the principal ideal sheaf `(f)`, and the
precomposition `G ⟶ (f)ᵏ G` with multiplication by `fᵏ`, which exists only because the ideal is
principal.

## Main definitions

* `principalIdealSheaf`: the ideal sheaf `(f)` generated by a global section `f`.
* `smulPowHom`: multiplication by `fᵏ`, as an endomorphism of an `𝒪_X`-module.
* `smulPowToIdealPowSmul`: **the missing precomposition** `G ⟶ (f)ᵏ G`, the factorization of
  multiplication by `fᵏ` through the subsheaf `(f)ᵏ G` of `G`.

## Main results

* `support_compl_principalIdealSheaf`: the complement of the support of `(f)` is `D(f)`. This is
  what makes the open that [Stacks, Tag 01YB] is stated over into a principal open.
* `exists_hom_app_eq_overApp_smul_pow` and its principal-open form
  `exists_hom_app_eq_overApp_smul_pow_basicOpen`: **the bridge.** For `θ : G|_{D(f)} ⟶ F|_{D(f)}`
  there are `k` and `ψ : G ⟶ F` with `ψ(g) = θ(fᵏ g)` on every open contained in `D(f)`.

## Implementation notes

The precomposition `G ⟶ Iᵏ G` does not exist for a general ideal sheaf `I`: `Iᵏ G` is a proper
subsheaf of `G` and nothing maps `G` into it. For a principal ideal it does, namely
multiplication by `fᵏ`, and that is precisely why the source argument chooses an `f` with
`D(f) ⊆ V` rather than working with the open `V` directly.

Multiplication by `fᵏ` is taken from
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.terminalSectionToEnd`, which gives multiplication by a section over a
terminal object of the site as an endomorphism of the identity functor; for the site of opens
of `X` the terminal object is `⊤`. Its commutativity hypothesis
`∀ U, IsMulCommutative (X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj U)` is not found by instance search, because the
rings of sections of `X.ringCatSheaf` are objects of `RingCat`, so it is supplied here as
`isMulCommutative_ringCatSheaf`.

`exists_hom_app_eq_overApp_smul_pow` takes the open `W` it works over as a variable together
with a proof that it is the complement of the support of `(f)`, rather than stating that
complement outright: the statement mentions `θ : G.over W ⟶ F.over W`, so rewriting `W` after
`θ` has been introduced is not available, while substituting the variable is.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01YB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01YB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01Y4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Y4)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPower Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerColimit

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.PrincipalIdealExtension

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- The rings of sections of the structure sheaf of a scheme, read as objects of `RingCat`, are
commutative. This is the hypothesis of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.terminalSectionToEnd`; instance
search does not find it because the commutative ring structure is attached to the `CommRingCat`
object `Γ(X, U)` rather than to its image in `RingCat`. -/
instance isMulCommutative_ringCatSheaf (U : (X.Opens)ᵒᵖ) :
    IsMulCommutative (X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj U) :=
  ⟨⟨fun a b => mul_comm (G := Γ(X, U.unop)) a b⟩⟩

/-- The restriction of a global section of `𝒪_X` to an open. -/
noncomputable abbrev restrictTop (f : Γ(X, ⊤)) (V : X.Opens) : Γ(X, V) :=
  X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : V ≤ ⊤)).op f

/-! ### Multiplication by a power of a global section -/

/-- **Multiplication by `fᵏ`**, as an endomorphism of an `𝒪_X`-module, for `f` a global section
of `𝒪_X`. -/
noncomputable def smulPowHom (G : X.Modules) (f : Γ(X, ⊤)) (k : ℕ) : G ⟶ G :=
  ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.terminalSectionToEnd X.ringCatSheaf (⊤ : X.Opens)
    isTerminalTop f) ^ k).asHom.app G

/-- Multiplication by `fᵏ` reads on sections as multiplication by the restriction of `fᵏ`. -/
theorem smulPowHom_app (G : X.Modules) (f : Γ(X, ⊤)) (k : ℕ) (V : X.Opens) (g : Γ(G, V)) :
    (smulPowHom G f k).app V g = restrictTop f V ^ k • g := by
  refine Eq.trans (Stacks.SheafOfModules.terminalSectionToEnd_pow_apply
    X.ringCatSheaf (⊤ : X.Opens) isTerminalTop f G k (op V) g) ?_
  congr 3

/-! ### The principal ideal sheaf -/

/-- The ideal sheaf `(f)` generated by a global section `f` of `𝒪_X`. -/
noncomputable def principalIdealSheaf (f : Γ(X, ⊤)) : X.IdealSheafData :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.span {f})

/-- **The complement of the support of `(f)` is the principal open `D(f)`.** This is what
identifies the open that [Stacks, Tag 01YB] extends over as a principal open, and hence what
makes the precomposition `G ⟶ (f)ᵏ G` below available. -/
theorem support_compl_principalIdealSheaf (f : Γ(X, ⊤)) :
    (principalIdealSheaf f).support.compl = X.basicOpen f := by
  apply Opens.ext
  show ((principalIdealSheaf f).support : Set X)ᶜ = _
  rw [principalIdealSheaf, Scheme.IdealSheafData.coe_support_ofIdealTop, Scheme.zeroLocus_span,
    Scheme.zeroLocus_singleton, compl_compl]

/-- The restriction of `f` to an affine open is a section of `(f)` there. -/
theorem restrictTop_mem_ideal_principalIdealSheaf (f : Γ(X, ⊤)) (V : X.affineOpens) :
    restrictTop f V.1 ∈ (principalIdealSheaf f).ideal V := by
  rw [principalIdealSheaf, Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop_ideal]
  exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ (Ideal.subset_span rfl)

/-! ### The precomposition `G ⟶ (f)ᵏ G` -/

/-- Over an affine open, `fᵏ g` is a section of `(f)ᵏ G`: the restriction of `fᵏ` lies in the
`k`-th power of the ideal of sections of `(f)`. -/
theorem smulPow_mem_idealPowerMultiple (G : X.Modules) (f : Γ(X, ⊤)) (k : ℕ)
    (V : X.affineOpens) (g : Γ(G, V.1)) :
    (smulPowHom G f k).app V.1 g ∈
      (idealPowerMultiple (principalIdealSheaf f) k G).toSubmodule.obj (op V.1) := by
  rw [smulPowHom_app]
  exact le_idealPowerMultiple_obj _ k G V
    (Submodule.smul_mem_smul (Ideal.pow_mem_pow
      (restrictTop_mem_ideal_principalIdealSheaf f V) k) Submodule.mem_top)

/-- **The precomposition `G ⟶ (f)ᵏ G`**: multiplication by `fᵏ`, factored through the subsheaf
`(f)ᵏ G` of `G`.

This is the map that is missing for a general ideal sheaf, and it is the reason the source
argument of [Stacks, Tag 01YB] picks a principal open: it turns the extension produced by that
tag, which is a morphism *out of* `Iᵏ G`, into a morphism out of `G`. -/
noncomputable def smulPowToIdealPowSmul (G : X.Modules) (f : Γ(X, ⊤)) (k : ℕ) :
    G ⟶ idealPowSmul (principalIdealSheaf f) k G :=
  factorThruOfForallAffineOpens _ (smulPowHom G f k) (smulPow_mem_idealPowerMultiple G f k)

/-- The precomposition `G ⟶ (f)ᵏ G` does not change the value of a section: as a section of `G`
it is `fᵏ g`. -/
theorem val_smulPowToIdealPowSmul_app (G : X.Modules) (f : Γ(X, ⊤)) (k : ℕ) (V : X.Opens)
    (g : Γ(G, V)) :
    (((smulPowToIdealPowSmul G f k).app V g).1 : Γ(G, V)) = restrictTop f V ^ k • g :=
  (val_factorThruOfForallAffineOpens_app _ _ _ V g).trans (smulPowHom_app G f k V g)

/-- The precomposition `G ⟶ (f)ᵏ G` followed by the inclusion of `(f)ᵏ G` into `G` is
multiplication by `fᵏ`. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
theorem smulPowToIdealPowSmul_ι (G : X.Modules) (f : Γ(X, ⊤)) (k : ℕ) :
    smulPowToIdealPowSmul G f k ≫ (idealPowerMultiple (principalIdealSheaf f) k G).ι =
      smulPowHom G f k :=
  factorThruOfForallAffineOpens_ι _ _ _

/-! ### The bridge -/

/-- **A morphism defined on `D(f)` extends to `X` after multiplication by a power of `f`.**

Let `X` be a Noetherian scheme, `f` a global section of `𝒪_X`, `G` a coherent and `F` a
quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module, and let `W` be the complement of the support of the ideal sheaf
`(f)`, that is, the principal open `D(f)`. Every morphism `θ : G|_W ⟶ F|_W` admits a `k` and a
morphism `ψ : G ⟶ F` of `𝒪_X`-modules with `ψ(g) = θ(fᵏ g)` on the sections over every open
contained in `W`.

This composes [Stacks, Tag 01YB] in the form
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerColimit.exists_homRestrict_eq`, which produces a morphism
out of `(f)ᵏ G`, with the precomposition `smulPowToIdealPowSmul`.

The open `W` is a variable constrained by `hW` rather than the complement itself because `θ` is
stated over it. -/
theorem exists_hom_app_eq_overApp_smul_pow [AlgebraicGeometry.IsNoetherian X]
    (f : Γ(X, ⊤)) (G F : X.Modules) [G.IsCoherent] [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    {W : X.Opens} (hW : (principalIdealSheaf f).support.compl = W)
    (θ : G.over W ⟶ F.over W) :
    ∃ (k : ℕ) (ψ : G ⟶ F), ∀ {V : X.Opens} (hV : V ≤ W) (g : Γ(G, V)),
      ψ.app V g = overApp θ hV (restrictTop f V ^ k • g) := by
  subst hW
  obtain ⟨k, φ, hφ⟩ := exists_homRestrict_eq (principalIdealSheaf f) G F θ
  refine ⟨k, smulPowToIdealPowSmul G f k ≫ φ, fun {V} hV g => ?_⟩
  have h := val_homRestrict_app (principalIdealSheaf f)
    (disjoint_supportCompl_support (principalIdealSheaf f)) φ
    (op (Over.mk (homOfLE hV))) (restrictTop f V ^ k • g)
  rw [hφ] at h
  refine Eq.trans ?_ h.symm
  show φ.app V ((smulPowToIdealPowSmul G f k).app V g) = _
  exact congrArg (φ.app V) (Subtype.ext (val_smulPowToIdealPowSmul_app G f k V g))

/-- **A morphism defined on `D(f)` extends to `X` after multiplication by a power of `f`**, in
the form that names the principal open. See `exists_hom_app_eq_overApp_smul_pow`. -/
theorem exists_hom_app_eq_overApp_smul_pow_basicOpen [AlgebraicGeometry.IsNoetherian X]
    (f : Γ(X, ⊤)) (G F : X.Modules) [G.IsCoherent] [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    (θ : G.over (X.basicOpen f) ⟶ F.over (X.basicOpen f)) :
    ∃ (k : ℕ) (ψ : G ⟶ F), ∀ {V : X.Opens} (hV : V ≤ X.basicOpen f) (g : Γ(G, V)),
      ψ.app V g = overApp θ hV (restrictTop f V ^ k • g) :=
  exists_hom_app_eq_overApp_smul_pow f G F (support_compl_principalIdealSheaf f) θ

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.PrincipalIdealExtension

end
